From 4fc91b56280c1411a2bea66dc114d84dc3f85905 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daryl Denson <9751141+denson9874@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:39:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] SystemUI: don't start AOD brighter than the dimmed screen

When the screen times out, DisplayPowerController dims it to
min(brightness - minimum dim amount, dim brightness).
DozeScreenBrightness applies the same formula to the doze brightness so
that AOD doesn't start brighter than the dimmed screen, but it starts
from the doze brightness, not the screen brightness. In auto-brightness
mode nothing clamps the doze brightness to the screen brightness, so in
a dark room AOD starts at the full dim brightness (0.05, about 120 nits
on the Pixel 11 Pro XL) right after the screen was dimmed to the minimum
(0.5 nits). The screen flashes bright for about half a second, until
the AOD light sensor reports and the brightness ramps down.

Take the lower of the doze brightness and the current screen brightness
before applying the dim formula, so AOD starts at or below the
brightness the screen was dimmed to.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../com/android/systemui/doze/DozeScreenBrightness.java   | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/doze/DozeScreenBrightness.java b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/doze/DozeScreenBrightness.java
index b7ca7351e..8fe948e77 100644
--- a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/doze/DozeScreenBrightness.java
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/doze/DozeScreenBrightness.java
@@ -429,6 +429,14 @@ public class DozeScreenBrightness extends BroadcastReceiver implements DozeMachi
                 && mState == DozeMachine.State.INITIALIZED;
         if (screenTurningOff
                 && mWakefulnessLifecycle.getLastSleepReason() == GO_TO_SLEEP_REASON_TIMEOUT) {
+            // DisplayPowerController dimmed the current screen brightness, not the doze
+            // brightness. In auto-brightness mode the doze brightness isn't clamped to the screen
+            // brightness, and in the dark the screen can be far below mScreenBrightnessDim, so
+            // AOD would start brighter than the dimmed screen until the light sensor reports.
+            final float screenBrightness = getScreenBrightness();
+            if (!Float.isNaN(screenBrightness)) {
+                brightness = Math.min(brightness, screenBrightness);
+            }
             return Math.max(
                     PowerManager.BRIGHTNESS_MIN,
                     // Use the lower of either the dim brightness, or the current brightness reduced
